{
	"name": "Sand Glider",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/time/day-night-sunset-sunrise.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You’re an experienced desert dweller, you know how to dress for the weather and how to move through the treacherous expanse of dunes and valleys.</p><ul><li><p>You gain proficiency in the Survival skill. If you already have proficiency, you gain an expertise die (to a maximum of 1d10.)</p></li><li><p>You have advantage on Survival checks related to tracking, foraging and waymaking while in Desert terrain, and your movement speed is increased by 10ft on such terrain. </p></li><li><p>You can travel to your full carrying capacity without suffering Fatigue or Strife caused by the heat, unless you’re wearing heavy armor, in which case the base Saving Throw DC applies. </p></li><li><p>When fighting in deserts or on sandy terrain, you impose disadvantage on opportunity attacks made against you.</p></li></ul>",
